      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Condensing pediculolaminar hypertrophy of mechanical origin is known as \"Dahu's sign\". Dahu's sign corresponds to hypertrophy of the vertebral hemi-arch found by CT scan and leads to suspicion of controlateral lysis of the isthmus. It is the CT scan equivalent of vertebral \"anisocorism\" by conventional radiology."},
